From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prokrypt <prokrypt@edited.us>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:53:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: spl: turn the instruction cache on

SPL runs with both caches off, so every instruction is fetched from
DRAM. On a Pinebook Pro (RK3399) the time from the end of TPL to the
start of U-Boot proper was 3.9 s, most of it SPL reading U-Boot and
TF-A (1.2 MB) from SPI flash in a polling loop: raising the SPI clock
from 10 to 25 MHz barely changed it.

On ARMv8 the instruction cache works with the MMU off, so enable it at
the start of board_init_f(). Turn it off and invalidate it again in
bl31_entry(), next to the existing dcache_disable(), so TF-A is entered
in the same state as before.
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 common/spl/spl_atf.c         |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
index 30be6404..12cea315 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <common.h>
+#include <cpu_func.h>
 #include <debug_uart.h>
 #include <dm.h>
 #include <hang.h>
@@ -112,6 +113,17 @@ void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && !CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SYS_ICACHE_OFF)
+	/*
+	 * SPL runs with both caches off, so every instruction is fetched
+	 * from DRAM. That made it take seconds on RK3399, most of it in
+	 * the loop that reads U-Boot and TF-A from SPI flash. The
+	 * instruction cache works with the MMU off; it is turned off again
+	 * before TF-A is entered (bl31_entry()).
+	 */
+	icache_enable();
+#endif
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_UART
 	/*
 	 * Debug UART can be used from here if required:
diff --git a/common/spl/spl_atf.c b/common/spl/spl_atf.c
index 2c102528..645bfd6b 100644
--- a/common/spl/spl_atf.c
+++ b/common/spl/spl_atf.c
@@ -205,6 +205,9 @@ static void bl31_entry(uintptr_t bl31_entry, uintptr_t bl32_entry,
 
 	raw_write_daif(SPSR_EXCEPTION_MASK);
 	dcache_disable();
+	/* Hand over with the instruction cache off as well, as before */
+	icache_disable();
+	invalidate_icache_all();
 
 	atf_entry(bl31_params, (void *)fdt_addr);
 }
